From bd9fa1339487317141f378abeffc85668f42f70f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Bryan <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:22:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] fix(plugin-mcp): version precondition per write, not
 per user (research v2.2)

Research v1 to v2.1 used, when ifUpdatedAt was left out, the version the
server remembered for the user. Two MCP clients sharing one key are the same
user, so one client's read or write refreshed the other's remembered version
and the other's stale write went through.

Every update and delete now carries the version its change is based on:
ifUpdatedAt is required in the advertised schema (a string with id, a map
{"<id>": "<updatedAt>"} for several documents). A document whose updatedAt is
no longer the one sent is refused with its current state, whoever changed it.
In a bulk call, a document the where matches but the map does not name is
refused as "no_version". The per-user memory is gone. Find keeps updatedAt in
its answer under any select, so the caller always has the version to send;
receipts already carry it. The default instructions say so. Collections with
timestamps off keep ifUpdatedAt optional and unchecked.

Tests: versionPrecondition.spec.ts (10), with an in-memory Payload stand-in
and a real MCP server and client (fakePayload.spec-utils.ts).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
